===Etymology 1===
{{wp|,+ (butterfly)}}
[[File:Stone wall with slate toppers - geograph.org.uk - 1379083.jpg|thumb|A stone '''wall''' ({{senseno|en|barrier|etym=0}}).]]
{{etymon|en|id=rampart|:inh|enm:wal<id:wall>}}
From {{inh|en|enm|wal}}, from {{inh|en|ang|weall|t=wall, dike, earthwork, rampart, dam, rocky shore, cliff}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*wall|t=wall, rampart, entrenchment}}, from {{der|en|la|vallum|t=wall, rampart, entrenchment, palisade}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*welH-|t=to turn, wind, roll}}.

Perhaps conflated with {{m|en|waw|t=a wall within a house or dwelling, a room partition}}, from {{noncog|enm|wawe}}, from {{noncog|ang|wāg}}, {{m|ang|wāh|t=an interior wall, divider}}, see {{l|en|waw}}.

Cognate with {{cog|frr|wal|t=wall}}, {{cog|stq|Waal|t=wall, rampart, mound}}, {{cog|nl|wal|t=wall, rampart, embankment}}, {{cog|de|Wall|t=rampart, mound, embankment}}, {{cog|sv|vall|t=mound, wall, bank}}. More at {{l|en|wallow}}, {{l|en|walk}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|barrier}} A [[rampart]] of earth, stones etc. built up for [[defensive]] purposes.
#: {{mero|en|terreplein|parapet|crenellation|banquette}}
# {{senseid|en|surrounding}} A structure built for [[defense]] surrounding a city, castle etc.
#: {{ux|en|The town '''wall''' was surrounded by a moat.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-06-08|volume=407|issue=8839|page=52|magazine=w:The Economist| title=[http://www.economist.com/news/international/21579039-chinas-growing-empire-ports-abroad-mainly-about-trade-not-aggression-new-masters The new masters and commanders]| passage=From the ground, Colombo’s port does not look like much. Those entering it are greeted by wire fences, '''walls''' dating back to colonial times and security posts. For mariners leaving the port after lonely nights on the high seas, the delights of the B52 Night Club and Stallion Pub lie a stumble away.}}
# {{senseid|en|structural}} Each of the substantial [[structure]]s acting either as the [[exterior]] of or [[division]]s within a structure.
#: {{ux|en|We're adding another '''wall''' in this room during the remodeling.&emsp; {{nowrap|The wind blew against the '''walls''' of the tent.}}}}
