===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|en|id=adjective|:inh|enm:warm|tree=1}}
{{root|en|ine-pro|*gʷʰer-|*wer-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|warm}}, {{m|enm|werm}}, from {{inh|en|ang|wearm}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*warm}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*warmaz}}, from one of:
* {{inh|en|ine-pro||*wór-mo-s}}, from {{suf|ine-pro|*wer-|t1=to burn|nocat=1}}, which is related to {{cog|hit|𒉿𒊏𒀀𒉌|tr=warāni|t=to burn}}, {{cog|hy|վառել||to burn, heat, warm}}, {{cog|cu|варити||to cook, boil}}.
* {{inh|en|ine-pro||*gʷʰor-mo-s}}, from the root {{m|ine-pro|*gʷʰer-||warm, hot}}, in which case cognate with {{cog|grc|θερμός}} (making perhaps a distant {{dbt|en|thermos|nocap=1}}), {{cog|la|formus}}, {{cog|sa|घर्म|tr=gharmá}}.
In any case cognate within Germanic to {{cog|fy|waarm}}, {{cog|stq|woorm}}, {{cog|nl|warm}}, {{cog|de|warm}}, {{cog|sv|varm}}, {{cog|is|varmur}}.

