====Usage notes====
Used as a second element of many personal names. It could be appended to mythical creatures as in {{l|ang|Ælfwine||elf friend}} ; or animals as in {{l|ang|Wulfwine||wolf friend}}; or inanimate objects as in {{l|ang|Goldwine||gold friend}}; or locations as in {{l|ang|Centwine||Kent friend}}; or features of nature as in {{l|ang|Sǣwine||sea friend}} and {{l|ang|Æsċwine||ash friend}}; or kinds of people as in {{l|ang|Pihtwine||Pict friend}} and {{l|ang|Bregowine||prince friend}}; or abstract concepts as in {{l|ang|Ēadwine||prosperity/happiness friend}} and {{l|ang|Bōtwine||repair/penance friend}}. It was also often used with adjectives, usually praising the owner of the name, as in {{l|ang|Beorhtwine||bright friend}} and {{l|ang|Ealdwine||old friend}}.

