#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Tax Reform Proposals: Hearing Before the Committee on Finance|
author={{w|Bob Packwood}}|publisher=United States. Congress. Senate. Committee on Finance|year=1985|page=52|text=I don't find the answers you have given will '''wash''' with the general public. And eventually, if they don't '''wash''', then these deductions will be gone.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=16 Apr 88|journal=Gay Community News|page=12|author=Chris Bull|title=PWA Group Struggles To Reach People of Color|text=Laureano singled out for criticism several board members who resisted the creation of the MAC and who suggested instead that the board deal with "reverse discrimination." "That doesn't '''wash'''," said Laureano. "It's just a knee-jerk reaction to what we are trying to achieve."}}
#* '''2012''', {{w|The Economist}}, Oct 13th 2012 issue, ''[http://www.economist.com/node/21564595 The Jordan and its king: As beleaguered as ever]''
#*: The king is running out of ideas as well as cash. His favourite shock-absorbing tactic—to blame his governments and sack his prime ministers—hardly '''washes'''.
