===Etymology 2===
[[Image:Boelge stor.jpg|thumb|The wave after a ferry (1)]]
From {{inh|en|enm|*wave}}, partially from {{m|enm|waven||to fluctuate, wave}} (see above) and partially from {{inh|en|enm|wawe}}, {{m|enm|waghe||wave}}, from {{inh|en|ang|wǣg||a wave, billow, motion, water, flood, sea}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*wēgaz||motion, storm, wave}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*weǵʰ-||to drag, carry}}. 
{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|frr|waag|t=wave}}, {{cog|fy|weach|t=wave}}, {{cog|nl|waag|t=wave}}, {{cog|de|Woge}}, {{m|de|Wooge|t=wave}}, {{cog|da|vove}}, {{m|da|våg|t=wave}}, {{cog|fo|vágur|t=bay}}, {{cog|is|vogur|t=bay}}, {{cog|nb|-}}, {{cog|nn|-}} and {{cog|sv|våg|t=wave}}, {{cog|got|𐍅𐌴𐌲𐍃|t=wave}}, {{cog|fr|vague|t=wave}} (from {{cog|non|vágr|t=ocean, sea; wave}}). See also {{l|en|waw}}.
